    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>KMnO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> acts as an oxidising agent. In neutral or faintly alkaline medium alkaline <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>KMnO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is reduced to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>MnO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><msubsup><mi>MnO</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>8</mn><msub><mi>MnO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><msubsup><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>OH</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math></p><p>The change in oxidation state of manganese in this reaction is from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math>. So,&nbsp; In this reaction overall change in oxidation state of manganese will be 3.</p></blockquote>"
